# #1929 (epic #1891 slice 1): the sdist must carry the tortoise.packs
# discovery stub so a wheel rebuilt from the sdist (pip install <sdist>,
# --no-binary :all: tooling) still ships the pack catalog. Without it, the
# sdist ships only the loose packs/ source files and the rebuilt wheel has
# ZERO tortoise/packs/ entries — the silent empty-registry defect (G1)
# resurfacing on the sdist install path. Verified 2026-08-28 (plan-verify
# gate): with this include, the sdist-rebuilt wheel ships all manifests.
include tortoise/packs/__init__.py
# #9231 review P2: the same trap, on the record's SCHEMA. `pyproject.toml` maps
# `tortoise.record_migrations` at `supabase/migrations` and ships the record's
# SQL as package data, so an INSTALLED `tortoise` carries the files
# `record_projection.table_columns()` parses (a wheel has no `supabase/` tree,
# so without them every armed live write raised before its first statement and
# the record stayed empty while the static wiring gate read green). The stub is
# discovered by `packages.find`, NOT owned by any package (`package-dir`
# remaps the package's sources to `supabase/migrations`), so the sdist does not
# pick it up on its own — measured: built the sdist without this line and
# `tortoise/record_migrations/__init__.py` was ABSENT while the 7 SQL files were
# present. A wheel rebuilt from that sdist would discover no package and ship
# ZERO record schema — the G1 silent-empty class above, on a path where the
# writer itself is the consumer.
include tortoise/record_migrations/__init__.py
